title: Trade War
text: The border lets nothing across square-on, and at the customs gate only what both sides have in common gets through. Green is easy. How does yellow cross with nothing taken off it?
trick: a diagonal wall stops straight beams but a slanting beam slips between its corners, and only a gate can turn a straight beam onto the slant. Yellow AND cyan pays the tariff and crosses as green; to cross whole, yellow must be split and gated with itself, because a beam ANDed with itself loses nothing
motif: a border: a diagonal wall across the whole board, the home side a street grid of open squares between occupied blocks, the far side occupied land with one target in each slanting line of sight
expect: merges>=2
